---
// OcrPipeline component - How document scanning works, in plain English
---

<section id="ocr-pipeline" class="relative bg-white py-20 border-t border-slate-200">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 sm:px-8">

    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl text-center">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-emerald-200 bg-[#ecfdf5] px-3.5 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-[#15803d] uppercase tracking-wider mb-3.5">
        Document Scanning
      </div>
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 sm:text-4xl">
        How scanning a document works.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-base text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
        Point your Android phone at a paper document — the app does the rest. No manual typing required.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- 3-step flow -->
    <div class="mt-12 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-3">

      <div class="relative rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/90 bg-white p-7 shadow-xs transition hover:shadow-md hover:border-slate-300">
        <div class="absolute -top-4 left-7 flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-[#15803d] text-sm font-bold text-white shadow-xs">1</div>
        <div class="flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-[#ecfdf5] text-2xl mt-2 mb-4">📸</div>
        <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-slate-900">Scan or Upload</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
          Use the Android app to take a photo of the paper document, or drag and drop a PDF into the desktop app.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="relative rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/90 bg-white p-7 shadow-xs transition hover:shadow-md hover:border-slate-300">
        <div class="absolute -top-4 left-7 flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-[#15803d] text-sm font-bold text-white shadow-xs">2</div>
        <div class="flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-[#eff6ff] text-2xl mt-2 mb-4">🔍</div>
        <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-slate-900">App Reads the Form</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
          The system automatically reads the student's name, LRN, birth date, and other details from the scanned image.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="relative rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/90 bg-white p-7 shadow-xs transition hover:shadow-md hover:border-slate-300">
        <div class="absolute -top-4 left-7 flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-[#15803d] text-sm font-bold text-white shadow-xs">3</div>
        <div class="flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-[#ecfdf5] text-2xl mt-2 mb-4">✅</div>
        <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-slate-900">Record is Saved</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
          The student record is saved to the school database and becomes instantly searchable from any teacher workstation.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

    <!-- CTA Banner -->
    <div class="mt-12 rounded-2xl border border-emerald-200/80 bg-gradient-to-br from-emerald-50/70 via-white to-slate-50 p-8 sm:p-10 text-center shadow-xs">
      <h3 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Digitize 100+ records in minutes.</h3>
      <p class="mt-2.5 text-base text-slate-600 max-w-xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
        Instead of manually typing student information one by one, staff can scan whole stacks of documents quickly and accurately.
      </p>
      <a
        href="#downloads"
        class="mt-6 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-xl bg-[#15803d] px-6 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-white shadow-md shadow-[#15803d]/15 hover:bg-[#166534] transition"
      >
        <svg class="h-4 w-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M4 16v1a3 3 0 003 3h10a3 3 0 003-3v-1m-4-4l-4 4m0 0l-4-4m4 4V4" />
        </svg>
        Get the App
      </a>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>
